cc 1.0.85..1.1.33: add the PowerPC Darwin targets to the macOS architecture table of apple_flags(). The unified
Apple handling introduced in 1.0.84 maps a macOS target's architecture to an AppleArchSpec and returns
"Unknown architecture for macOS target." for anything but i686/x86_64/aarch64 (arm64e from 1.1.31), and it runs
for every `-apple-` target, so every build script that compiles C through these cc versions fails on
powerpc-apple-darwin (ring 0.17.8 in hackernews-tui 0.13.5: `error occurred: Unknown architecture for macOS
target.`). On macOS the spec's -m32/-m64 string is not emitted (only -mmacosx-version-min=, whose default the
mrustc PortGroup already points at macosx_deployment_target); powerpc64's -m64 comes from the generic non-MSVC
path. 1.1.34 removed the table (the Clang path passes --target, GCC gets -mmacosx-version-min= only), so later
versions need nothing; 1.0.84 (yanked, spells it ArchSpec::Device) is not covered. The hunk carries one line of
context on purpose: the line before `match arch_str {` changed in 1.1.32 (`if target.os == "macos"`) and the
line after `"i686"` in 1.1.31 (`| "arm64e"`), while these two lines are identical from 1.0.85 to 1.1.33
(dry-run on every crates.io version 1.0.83..1.2.5: exact application 1.0.85..1.1.33 only).

--- a/src/lib.rs
+++ b/src/lib.rs
@@ -2720,2 +2720,4 @@
             match arch_str {
+                "powerpc" => AppleArchSpec::Device("-m32"),
+                "powerpc64" => AppleArchSpec::Device("-m64"),
                 "i686" => AppleArchSpec::Device("-m32"),
